test.tsx:5:11: `keyframes()` cannot compile here on React Native: the build reads the keyframes written in the call. Fix: pass one object of keyframes, such as `keyframes({ from: { opacity: 0 }, to: { opacity: 1 } })`
test.tsx:6:12: `keyframes()` cannot compile here on React Native: the build reads the keyframes written in the call. Fix: pass one object of keyframes, such as `keyframes({ from: { opacity: 0 }, to: { opacity: 1 } })`
test.tsx:7:11: `keyframes` can only be called on React Native: the build compiles each call into styles. Fix: call it where the styles are used
test.tsx:8:23: `<Box>` cannot use `animationName` on React Native: `animationName` takes the keyframes `keyframes()` gives on React Native, not a name. Fix: pass what `keyframes({ ... })` gives
test.tsx:8:44: `<Box>` cannot use `animation` on React Native: react-native-reanimated reads the longhands of `animation`, and the keyframes as an object `keyframes()` gives. Fix: write `animationName={keyframes({ ... })}` with `animationDuration` and the other longhands
test.tsx:9:50: `<Box>` cannot use `transition` on React Native: react-native-reanimated animates a `style` object, and a press, hover or focus style makes the `style` a function. Fix: animate an element inside the pressable one
